--What are functions in SQL??
--Functions=Built-in operations that perform a specific task inside a query
--Common built in function:
	--ROUND(), Round a number to n decimals. Ex. SELECT ROUND(3.14159,2)  Result: 3.14
--CEIL()/FLOOR(), Round up or down.   Ex. SELECT CEIL(2.1) --> 3    SELECT FLOOR(3.2) --> 3

--Text Functions
--UPPER(text), converts text to uppercase  Ex. SELECT UPPER(category)
--LOWER(text), converts to lowercase   Ex. SELECT LWER(product_name)
--LENGTH(text), converts character count  Ex. SELECT LENGTH(product_name)

--Date Functions:
--NOW(), current timestamp   Ex. SELECT NOW()
--CURRENT_DATE, today's day   Ex. SELECT CURRENT_DATE
--AGE(), returns the difference between two dates   Ex. SELECT AGE('2025-10-20','2000-05-15');   Output: 25 years 5 mos 5 days
--Date functions are often used for reports or logs

